ls{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/deployments","created_at":"2012-12-07T13:30:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T11:48:01Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-11T20:11:30Z","git_url":"git://github.com/python/mypy.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:python/mypy.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy","homepage":"https://www.mypy-lang.org/","size":77161,"stargazers_count":20064,"watchers_count":20064,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":3065,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3124,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Consider the following example:\r\n\r\n```python3\r\nfrom typing import TypeVar, Generic\r\nimport attr\r\n\r\nclass V:\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nclass W:\r\n    pass\r\n\r\nT = TypeVar(\"T\", V, W)\r\n\r\n@attr.s(auto_attribs=True)\r\nclass A(Generic[T]):\r\n    v: T\r\n\r\nreveal_type(A(W()))\r\n```\r\n\r\nMy expectation here would be a revealed type of `A[W*]`, which I *do* get.\r\n\r\nBut I also get an error on the `@attr.s` definition:\r\n```\r\nThe erased type of self 'V*' is not a supertype of its class 'A[T`1]'\r\nThe erased type of self 'W*' is not a supertype of its class 'A[T`1]'\r\n```\r\n\r\nif I remove the constraints on `T`, (i.e. `T = TypeVar(\"T\")`) then the errors go away.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/5542/reactions","total_co